{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now Bronze Bar ×1 in inventory! So the reward was granted after closing the summary dialog. Fine. Not a bug. Good thing I checked.\n\nSo crafting works: 1 bar produced, +6 XP. The inventory shows Bronze Bar ×1. Great.\n\nNote the Smithing list row still \"Owned: 0\" was shown before summary dismissal; now maybe it updates. Not an issue.\n\nNow XP display: actual +6. The dialog says +6 for 1 bar. For 3 bars, displayed +18; actual likely floor(6.2*3)=18? Let's verify by crafting 3 bars? That would take 2m48s game time, which real time might be ~4 min. Not worth. Since actual 1 bar gave 6 (not 6.2), the internal per-bar XP might be 6.2 rounded down at award (6). Then 3 bars could award 18.6→18. Dialog matches. So no bug in XP readout for these values. But what about the \"simpler text formatter\" bug — maybe it's about large totals with thousands separators. E.g., a batch of 180 bars: 180*6.2=1116, formatted maybe \"1116 XP\" vs \"1,116 XP\"? The simpler formatter might drop comma separators. Or it might show \"1.116\" with decimal? Hmm.\n\nLet's look for a bigger XP total. At Smithing level 19, we can craft maybe many Bronze Arrow Tips (15 per craft) using bars. XP per tip? If 15 arrow tips per craft, requires 1 bar, duration maybe 26s? Could produce XP like 6.2? Total small.\n\nCrafting skill items: Silver Ring etc require bars we don't have. But we might smelt bronze only. How to get silver bars? Need silver ore, mining level 20, player has 50. Could mine silver ore session—60 ores/session, would take 60 actions * ~? game time. Not ideal.\n\nAlternatively, check Smithing item with high per-craft XP that requires only ore? Bronze bar itself. After level 19, could we smelt Iron Bar? Iron ore not in inventory (0). Need mine.\n\nMaybe the batch dialog's XP formatter issue shows only with totals >= 1000 or fractional. We can apply the \"Max\" of copper/tin 24 → 148. If we get more tin via mining... no.\n\nWait, the crafting dialog for Bronze Arrow Tips: \"×15 per craft\", uses 1 Bronze Bar. Quantity maybe up to 1 bar. XP total maybe e.g., \"×15 per craft\" * 0.4? Unknown.\n\nLet's first use the Bronze Bar we crafted to craft a Bronze Dagger or Arrow Tips, to test the batch dialog for a different item and maybe XP decimals. Bronze Dagger: 1 bar, Owned 1. XP? Let's see. But that would consume the bar; fine.\n\nBefore that, check \"Owned\" update in Smithing screen. Go Skills > Smithing."}
