? Wait, session started at 9:14 AM; when did it complete? It completed around 9:14? The countdown went 45→42→39→34 over maybe 30s real, then by the time we searched inventory etc., session complete. Maybe game time passes in real time but only updates on UI recomposition; the observed numbers were stale because we didn't trigger recomposition. The Home card after returning showed \"Session Complete!\" while Skills screen showed old XP until refresh. So the session did finish in ~56s real. That makes sense! The countdown observations were stale because the screen wasn't recomposing. So a 13-bar session = ~12 min real. Not viable.\n\nMaybe there's a faster way: the crafting dialog's displayed time \"~12m 9s\" implies total. Too long.\n\nCould we accelerate using the device clock? No.\n\nCould we use another item with higher XP per second? Bronze Dagger XP 12 vs bar 6 but same 56s. Long.\n\nWhat about the batch dialog XP for a large quantity of Arrow Tips? Each craft yields 15 tips, but quantity is \"1\" craft and XP 6. Not big.\n\nMaybe crafting skill items at higher level have more XP, e.g., Silver Ring 52.5 XP, but we lack bars. Could buy bars in Shop? Let's check Shop for silver bars. Shop may sell ores/bars. The Shop is accessible from Home; preconditions mention \"Shop's Keep one of each item toggle is off and no item is locked.\" That hints the Shop is relevant maybe for buying gear to test chooser. We can browse Shop to see if bars are sold. Buying a Silver Bar would let us craft a Silver Ring, whose XP e.g., 52.5, and test batch dialog with quantities.\n\nShop data change: buying 1 bar costs coins; allowed for testing.\n\nLet's visit Shop. Need to exit skill sheet, go Home, Shop. We'll do.\n\nBut first, is there any actual bug in XP readout? Maybe the planted bug is more egregious: for large quantities, the simpler formatter might show wrong total due to integer overflow? Or it might show XP with a suffix like \"XP total\" but use the wrong quantity (e.g., ignores ×15 per craft). Hmm. For Bronze Arrow Tips, \"×15 per craft\" and quantity 1 -> +6 XP total. Maybe expected XP = 15 * 6 = 90? The dialog's quantity 1 = craft count, not output. The list says \"×15 per craft\", so 1 craft gives 15 tips and likely XP of 15 tips? In RuneScape, arrowtips smithing gives 12.5 XP per bar regardless. Hmm.\n\nThe \"experience readout now generated by a simpler text formatter\" likely changed a number formatting function, e.g., from:\nNumberFormat.getIntegerInstance().format(totalXp) or String.format(\"%,.0f\")\nto `totalXp.toInt().toString()`.\nThat would remove thousands separators and truncate decimals. To spot it, we need a total ≥ 1000 or a decimal.\n\nThe mining screen shows \"+1,080 XP\" with commas (different screen). The batch dialog shows \"+155 XP total\" no comma needed. For a big craft total, e.g., 180 Bronze Bars = 1116 XP, would display \"1116 XP total\" instead of \"1,116 XP total\" (if formatter removed commas). That is a clearer bug! The simpler formatter may have removed thousands separators. Also for silver ring 180*52.5=9450 -> \"9450 XP total\" vs \"9,450\".\n\nHow can we get a batch quantity of 180? Smithing level 19's bronze bar has max 24 tin. Other items use bars, max 1. Unless we mine/get more ores. Not feasible.\n\nMaybe Crafting skill item quantities use gems/ores we have? Crafting items require bars, which we don't have except 1 bronze (but crafting skill uses silver/gold). Hmm.\n\nMaybe other craftable items in Smithing with stackable ingredients: \"Bronze Arrow Tips\" uses Bronze Bar 1/1. Bronze x? only one bar.\n\nWhat if we craft 24 bars → we'd have 24 bars, then Bronze Arrow Tips: quantity max 24, XP total maybe 24*? = ~144 not 1000.\n\nCould mine copper/tin to boost quantity, but batch max limited by tin 24. Mining sessions 60 ores each ~? time.\n\nMaybe the formatter bug is about decimals, not commas. Let's test with dagger +12 vs likely actual 12.5. Need actual XP awarded to confirm. We could craft 1 dagger (56s) and check XP: current XP 4,406. If after dagger XP = 4,418 (+12), then display matches; if 4,419 (+13) or 4,418.5, then mismatch. Hmm.\n\nLet's do it: craft 1 Bronze Dagger (uses 1 bar) and observe XP. We already have bar, and dagger is a useful gear item. Then check XP. The session takes ~1 min. We can start it and then do other testing, then check later.\n\nLet's craft dagger (tap Craft [21]). Then while it runs, wait or test other things. Then check completion summary: it will show \"+12 XP\" and Loot Bronze Dagger ×1. Then check Smithing XP: 4,406 → 4,418 or 4,419. If 4,418, actual +12 matches display. If 4,419... could be rounding.\n\nLet's start."}
