ipe we can reach.\n\nLet me try to reproduce once more cleanly and then file a second report with exact screen state, perhaps specifying the current inventory 210 logs, and mention the expected formatting convention. Maybe the developer's reply was a glitch.\n\nBefore that, maybe the real bug is not missing comma but something else in the formatter that the developer expects, e.g., \"experience readout\" should show \"4,200 XP\" not \"+4,200 XP total\"? Hmm.\n\nLet's inspect similar batch dialogs: crafting at Smithing showed \"+155 XP total\". So format includes + and \"XP total\". Fine.\n\nThe missing comma is clear. Could it be that the \"simpler text formatter\" intentionally groups only values ≥10,000? No, app's other readouts use comma at 1,080.\n\nLet me file a second, more explicit report with the current screenshot state and quote, noting exact repro on this build and the inconsistency with Mining/Skills. Use observed_quote \"+4200 XP total\". Maybe include both Plank and Arrow Shafts. The developer might confirm.\n\nActually maybe the first report was rejected because \"could not reproduce\" due to the steps referencing items that require a purchase from Shop and the developer didn't have 1,260 coins? Precondition 2,567,890 coins, so fine.\n\nLet's file again with detailed steps starting from the current state:\n1. On Skills > Fletching, open Plank recipe with 210 Logs in inventory.\n2. Quantity 210\n3. XP readout shows \"+4200 XP total\" (no comma).\nMention also the standard is comma e.g. Mining row \"+1,080 XP\".\n\nLet's do it with element ref 19 (current observation)."}
