{"type": "thinking", "text": "Bronze Dagger gone. So chooser reload works. No bug there in this scenario.\n\nHmm. What could be the gear chooser bug? Maybe it's about inventory items that are *equipped*: selling blocked. Candidate list includes equipped items, which is possibly intended to allow swapping.\n\nMaybe the bug is that the chooser loads candidates from inventory but fails to include items received via gear sets? Hmm.\n\nLet's read the change note again: \"Gear and equipment slot chooser: candidate items are now loaded from the inventory each time it opens.\" This could mean previously the chooser showed all items (regardless of ownership), now it loads from inventory. The planted bug might be that it reloads from inventory but *doesn't filter by slot correctly*, e.g., the Weapon (Atk) chooser includes Bronze Dagger and Iron Sword (correct). The Body chooser includes only platebodies (correct). What about \"Cape\"? It included Agility Cape and Mercantile Cape (both capes, correct). Head: helmets. Boots: Bronze Boots. Legs: none. Ring: none. Necklace: none. Shield: none.\n\nMaybe filter by slot fails for some specific item: \"Steel Full Helmet\" vs \"Mithril Med Helmet\" both head. \"Gilded Platebody\" body. Slayer Platebody body. Good.\n\nWhat about \"Iron Sword (Atk)\" vs \"Basic Staff (Magic)\" classification? Weapon (Magic) shows Basic Staff; Weapon (Atk) shows Iron Sword. Bronze Dagger (Atk) gone after sell. Good.\n\nMaybe the bug is that the chooser includes items with unmet requirements as equippable. E.g., Gilded Platebody requires Defense 60; player has 70, so meets. Mithril Med Helmet req 30, meets. All meet requirements. Can't test unmet reqs without higher-level items? We could artificially add via debug? No.\n\nMaybe the candidate list doesn't show item *quantity*, so if you have multiple swords you can't tell. Not a bug.\n\nPotential bug: candidate items loaded from inventory *each time* but the \"equipped\" state isn't reflected; the chooser shows \"Equip\" for the item already equipped (Iron Sword, Gilded Platebody). That's a UX bug but maybe intended. Hmm, but \"candidate items\" typically exclude currently equipped. Yet clicking it is a no-op (tested). Not a functional bug.\n\nCould the bug be that after changing equipment, the chooser still lists the old item? We tested Gilded body after unequip/equip: list always included all bodies, which is right since none sold. Hmm.\n\nLet's look at another angle: maybe the gear chooser candidate list is *empty* for some slots because inventory loading is asynchronous, e.g., first open after app start shows no items. We could force-stop/relaunch? open_app doesn't reset data but brings to foreground. We can't force stop. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the bug is when opening a slot while in a different combat style, the candidates loaded are for the wrong style (e.g., Weapon (Atk) chooser shows Magic weapon). We tested Attack chooser shows Iron Sword only, Magic chooser shows Basic Staff. Fine.\n\nMaybe the bug involves the \"Equip Best Gear\" button: it equips from inventory each time, maybe it equips items with unmet requirements? All meet.\n\nLet's check the \"Boots\" chooser: it should list Bronze Boots and maybe other boots in inventory? Inventory only Bronze Boots. Fine.\n\nGiven the difficulty, perhaps the planted gear bug is elsewhere: e.g., equipping a two-handed weapon or shield conflict, not in our data.\n\nMaybe the \"Profile link into combat gear\" is actually the bug we found, and the \"Gear slot chooser\" change is fine. Not every changed item must have a bug. The task says sweep these areas; there may be 2 bugs. We found one; perhaps one more (formatter) but dev couldn't reproduce. Maybe the mining sort has a bug that we haven't noticed due to type. Let's re-examine mining order including quest icons: The list showed Rune Essence (1), Copper (1), Tin (1), Stone (10), Iron (15), Silver (20), Coal (30), Gold (40). Sorted ascending. But what if the intended order sh