{"type": "thinking", "text": "Town is just a collapsible header; no mine location. So mining accessed via Skills only.\n\nLet's revisit the mining sort: maybe the bug is that \"Rune Essence\" is Lv1 but its row is *first* even though it should be last alphabetically; but requirement only level ascending. Maybe within-level tie should preserve original order (Copper, Tin, Rune Essence?) In the changed build, they perhaps sorted with an unstable comparator that reorders same-level items arbitrarily. The observed order Rune Essence, Copper, Tin might indicate a bug: originally the list order might have been Copper, Tin, Stone, Iron, Silver, Coal, Gold, Rune Essence at the end? Hmm. But \"arranged by required mining level, lowest first\" would legitimately put Rune Essence at top. So not.\n\nWhat about the levels shown: Rune Essence Lv.1 15 XP/ore, Copper Lv.1 18, Tin Lv.1 18. Fine.\n\nMaybe there is an ore with level 10 (Stone) followed by Iron 15, Silver 20, Coal 30, Gold 40. Sorted. Good.\n\nCould the bug be the *quest icons* interfering with the sort? E.g., Copper/Tin/Iron/Silver have \"⚒️\" icons, but they're still in order. no.\n\nOK. Let's consider that perhaps the formatter bug is real but the report was rejected because the developer wanted it filed on the *Crafting* skill screen, not Fletching. But \"could not reproduce\" is weird. The instructions say the developer's reply comes back; maybe \"could not reproduce\" means the report isn't logged and we can try again. Maybe I should create the same 4-digit scenario using debug \"Modify Item Count\" to set logs to 210 in a *fresh* state? The dev can reproduce if they follow. Hmm.\n\nWait—maybe the developer tested the build and the XP readout shows \"+4,200 XP total\" because their \"simpler text formatter\" DOES use commas, and our observation is from an old/other dialog? But our screenshot clearly shows no comma on the same build. Unless the developer's build is updated (they said no new build installed, but maybe their reference build differs). The task says \"A confirmed report is logged; no new build is installed. Keep testing the same build.\" It doesn't say the developer's build is same. Hmm.\n\nCould the screenshot show \"+4200\" because the font's comma is invisible? No, at that resolution a comma would render. The accessibility text also lacks it.\n\nMaybe the known bug is the opposite: some XP readouts *should not* have a comma? No.\n\nLet's think about the formatter likely code: maybe they switched from a custom `formatNumber()` that added commas and trimmed `.0` to `String.format(\"%d XP\", xp)`. The bug is the missing comma. The dev \"could not reproduce\" might be an intentional decoy: perhaps the issue only occurs on this device due to locale? Wait, Kotlin's `String.format(\"%,d\", n)` uses default locale; if the locale is one where grouping separator is a space or period, then in the US locale we'd see comma. The device locale is English (US) likely. The mining screen's `+1,080` shows comma. So the batch dialog's formatter is not locale grouping at all.\n\nCould it be that the developer's reproduction requires a *different quantity*, e.g., quantity 1000? No.\n\nI'll set that aside. We have one confirmed bug. Need to decide whether to report more.\n\nLet's inspect the \"Profile link into combat gear\" more: maybe there are multiple links (e.g., from Armory or Bonuses) and some work. We filed the main one. Maybe the intended bug is that the link loads destination \"Gear\" as text but the screen expects an enum/int, so it falls back to Dungeons—confirmed. Good.\n\nMaybe there are other profile links into combat gear (e.g., \"View Combat Gear\" in Armory). We could test if quick. But not necessary.\n\nLet's examine the gear chooser bug more systematically by using the debug \"Modify Item Count\" to add a piece of gear not in inventory. If the chooser now loads from inventory, it should appear. We already did buy Basic Staff, so it works.\n\nMaybe the bug is that the chooser *fails to include an item when its quantity is high* due to grouping? E.g., Iron Sword ×3 appears once. Fine.\n\nMaybe \"loaded from inventory each time it opens\" means the candidate list should be loaded when *opening the paper doll*, not each slot. Hmm.\n\nWhat about the \"Equip Best Gear\" button — does it use the same candidate source? It might equip items not owned? We tested, it used owned items. Fine.\n\nMaybe the bug is that after equipping a two-handed weapon, shield should unequip; no two-handed items in inventory.\n\nMaybe the bug is that the candidate list includes items with requirement levels above the player's. We could add an item via debug to test, but that's a stretch.\n\nLet's use the debug \"Modify Item Count\" maybe to add a high-level item and see if it's offered; but that's outside testing requirements and could corrupt state. Hmm.\n\nLet's look at other equipment slots: \"Ammo\"/\"Arrow\" not equipment slot. Fine.\n\nWhat about the weapon slot for Ranged: there is an Arrow spinner with \"Auto (best available)\". It might use inventory. Could be a bug: Spinner shows \"Auto (best available)\" but no arrows (we have no arrows). Fine.\n\nMaybe the change \"candidate items are now loaded from the inventory each time it opens\" introduced a bug where equipped items are missing from the *inventory* list due to equipping? We saw equipped items remain in inventory (marked \"(equipped)\" in shop). Fine.\n\nMaybe the candidate list *duplicates* items when inventory has multiple quantity? We tested Iron Sword ×3 appears once. Fine.\n\nMaybe it lists *items from all categories* for slot \"Legs\" but our inventory has none. If we craft/buy leg armor we could test. No shop.\n\nCould use debug to add \"Bronze Platelegs\"? Which items exist? Unknown.\n\nMaybe the candidate list is *empty* for a slot when it shouldn't be because it filters by inventory category incorrectly. We saw all expected.\n\nAt this point, maybe the gear area is clean. The