{"type": "thinking", "text": "Aha! Now the Skills screen shows a \"Session Active\" card at top with \"Abandon Session\" and \"[Debug] Finish Now\". Great. So when a session is active, the Skills screen header changes; our earlier observations didn't capture it because we opened skills while sessions were maybe done.\n\nWe can test mining session UI:\n- \"Abandon Session\" [5]\n- \"[Debug] Finish Now\" [6] (a debug button—maybe use to finish instantly; that's a debug tool, acceptable? It would let us test session completion quickly! We could use it to test mining session rewards and maybe crafting batch actual XP. But using debug to finish sessions alters data, but testing requires. It's in the app. Could be very useful to test the formatter/actual XP for 3 bars without waiting.)\n\nWait: \"[Debug] Finish Now\" is a debug action that instantly completes the session. Using it to test the actual XP award for a batch would resolve the fractional/rounding questions. But is that \"changing data outside what testing requires\"? It's provided in the app; using it for QA is within testing. We already used debug Set XP dialog but didn't change. Hmm.\n\nCould we use Finish Now on the mining session to test rewards: it would award 60 Rune Essence and 900 XP instantly. That changes Mining XP/ores significantly (adds 60 essence, 900 XP). Maybe too much data change. But we can then abandon? Finish is one-way. Better to Abandon Session for mining and use Finish Now on a *small* crafting session (1 bar) we've already effectively tested. For batch XP testing (3 bars), we could start a 3-bar session, then Finish Now to see actual XP gain and loot. That would resolve the truncation issue. But it would add 3 bars, 18 or 20 XP. Small and acceptable.\n\nLet's do that! But first, abandon the mining session to restore no-session state (precondition). Tap \"Abandon Session\" [5]. Does it ask for confirmation? Let's tap."}
