{"type": "text", "text": "The device bridge died mid-sweep (`BrokenPipeError` on every tool, including `sign_off`), so I could not complete the final verification or sign off. Here is the state of the sweep:\n\n## Confirmed and logged\n**Profile → Gear → \"View Combat Gear\" navigates to the wrong Combat section**\n- Steps: Profile → Gear → tap \"View Combat Gear\".\n- Expected: Combat screen opens on the **Gear** tab.\n- Observed: Combat opens on the **Dungeons** tab (\"Dungeons\" selected, \"DUNGEONS\" header). Reproduced twice; developer replied \"confirmed and logged.\"\n\n## Reported but not accepted by the developer\n**Batch-dialog XP readout formatting**\n- Fletching > Plank with 210 logs showed **\"+4200 XP total\"** instead of \"+4,200 XP total\" (screenshot-verified); Arrow Shafts showed \"+1050 XP total\". Other screens use grouped values (\"+1,080 XP\", \"4,418 / 4,470 XP\").\n- Smithing > Bronze Bar at quantity 3 showed **\"+18 XP total\"** for 18.6 exact (6.2/bar); quantity 2 and 4 showed \"+12\" (12.4) and \"+24\" (24.8). Developer replied \"could not reproduce\" both times.\n\n## Repro not fileable before the outage\n- Home's active-session card is clipped by the bottom navigation bar (the \"Assigned: 3 Bronze Bar\" line is visually cut in half).\n- Screenshot evidence was captured.\n\n## Areas that appeared clean\n- **Mining screen:** ore list is level-ascending (Rune Essence/Copper/Tin Lv1, Stone 10, Iron 15, Silver 20, Coal 30, Gold 40); owned counts and \"Add to Session Queue\" state agreed with the inventory/session state; abandoning a mining session restored the prior XP/ore state.\n- **Gear/equipment:** Body/Head/Cape/Boots/Weapon (Atk/Magic/Ranged/Str)/tool choosers all matched current inventory; newly bought Basic Staff appeared in the Magic weapon chooser, sold Bronze Daggers disappeared; equipping/unequipping updated DEF correctly and survived leaving/re-entering the screen and rotating the device.\n\nBecause the tool server is unreachable, I could not reopen the completed session summary, finish the 3-bar/actual-XP comparison, or call `sign_off`."}
